    ]
  }
}
</pdd-interface>

% You are an expert Python engineer. Write `pdd/github_guard.py`.

<include>context/python_preamble.prompt</include>

% Role and scope

Provide one dependency-light, deterministic policy boundary for GitHub access
and authentication. This module performs no network or subprocess operation
other than locating the `gh` executable when access is allowed.

% Vocabulary

- **local-only**: `PDD_LOCAL_ONLY` has a case-insensitive truthy value from
  `1`, `true`, `yes`, or `on`.
- **GitHub-auth opt-in**: `PDD_ALLOW_GITHUB_AUTH` has a truthy value and
  local-only is false.
- **local agent instruction**: an instruction carrying a local-source marker
  (`local:`, `local-intent:`, `pdd-local://`, or repository owner `local`).

<contract_rules>
R1 (MUST): `local_only_enabled` recognizes exactly the documented truthy values after trimming and case folding.
R2 (MUST): `github_access_allowed` is false in local-only mode and true otherwise; `require_github_access` raises `GitHubAccessDisabled` with an actionable local-work-item message when false.
R3 (MUST): `github_auth_opted_in` is true only when `PDD_ALLOW_GITHUB_AUTH` is truthy and local-only is false.
R4 (MUST): `find_gh` returns None without calling `shutil.which` in local-only mode and otherwise returns `shutil.which("gh")`.
R5 (MUST): `instruction_is_local` recognizes local work-item and local-intent markers without classifying an ordinary GitHub issue URL as local.
R6 (MUST): `localize_agent_instruction` leaves non-local instructions byte-for-byte unchanged.
R7 (MUST): For a local instruction, `localize_agent_instruction` appends a highest-priority final policy that forbids `gh`, GitHub API/network access, GitHub comments/issues/pull requests, and GitHub authentication, and requires reports to be returned to the orchestrator for local persistence.
R8 (MUST): Re-localizing an already localized instruction is idempotent.
R9 (MUST NOT): Local-only mode may not be overridden by `PDD_ALLOW_GITHUB_AUTH`, `PDD_ALLOW_INTERACTIVE`, a configured GitHub Copilot model, or the presence of cached credentials.
</contract_rules>

% Deliverables

- Code: `pdd/github_guard.py`
- Tests: `tests/test_github_guard.py`
